The emucap direct libretro host, build recipe, documentation, and original
adapter glue are licensed GPL-2.0-or-later, the project default.

The pinned NP2kai source is downloaded into the ignored work tree and retains
its own file and component licenses. Its repository root is MIT licensed, but
the full source tree contains additional BSD, zlib, GPL, and custom notices.
The supported build profile excludes the components named in upstream.lock
and records both its compiled-source manifest and the complete upstream notice
inventory. Those upstream notices remain authoritative for upstream code and
must accompany any redistribution of a built core or corresponding source.

This repository does not distribute the NP2kai source archive, generated core,
firmware, rhythm samples, or game media. See ../../NOTICE, upstream.lock, and
README.md for the pinned source, supported build profile, and redistribution
boundary.

The full GPL-2.0 text is at ../../licenses/GPL-2.0.txt and online at
https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/gpl-2.0.html.
